<title>UK: BANK OF IRELAND SETS $150 MLN 10-YEAR FRN.</title>
<headline>BANK OF IRELAND SETS $150 MLN 10-YEAR FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue was announced by joint lead managers J.P. Morgan and Salomon Brothers.  BORROWER   BANK OF IRELAND</p>
<p> AMT    $150 MLN	BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY	.SEP.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN   **+25 BP    PAY DATE    04.SEP.97</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A2	  ISS PRICE  99.945    FULL FEES   0.40</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   A-	  REOFFER    99.945</p>
<p> NOTES    **UNTIL SEP.02 WHEN COUPON STEPS UP TO 3M LIBOR +75 BP</p>
<p>		IF NOT CALLED AT PAR</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS US/UK/IE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 1</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  IRELAND   TAX PROVS   STD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.20	SELL CONC  0.20	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
